From b524394cdb54309a625967ff3d234ae19de8e768 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DevShon1976 <devshon1976@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 16 Jul 2026 02:45:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Extend generative playbook to FinOps, Insurance,
 Construction, RE, Legal, BPO
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Backend (server.js):
- buildPlaybookPrompt(vertical) replaces the hardcoded HC-only
  PLAYBOOK_PROMPT. Each vertical gets a role + domain hint (e.g.
  'FinOps analyst' / 'GL reconciliation, AP/AR, budget variance')
  so the model grounds itself in the right vocabulary instead of
  defaulting to medical-billing language for every vertical.
- Added PLAYBOOK_FALLBACK_STEPS_{FO,INS,CON,RE,LEG,BPO}, tailored
  per-vertical wording for the same 7 checkStatus categories the
  HC fallback already used (DENIAL_RISK/AUTH_BLOCK/PAYMENT_BLOCK/
  COMPLIANCE_BLOCK/LEGAL_HOLD/DOCUMENTATION_BLOCK/ACTIVE).
- /api/doc-router/playbook now accepts an optional  field.
  Omitted or unrecognized -> defaults to 'hc', so this is fully
  backward compatible with the existing HC call path (#219/#220).

Frontend (tsm-doc-search-multi.html):
- New openGenNodeWithDoc(docId, vertical) — same generative-playbook
  pattern as openHcNodeWithDoc, generalized:
    - checkStatus derivation factored into deriveCheckStatus() (same
      logic openHcNodeWithDoc already used inline — these code-prefix
      conventions are shared across verticals in the seed data, not
      HC-specific).
    - Node resolution (resolveGenNodeId) matches doc.sourceNode or the
      last resolvable entry in doc.routing against that vertical's
      real node map, falling back to the vertical's own war-room node.
    - Navigation reads the real route already stored on
      VERTICALS[v].nodes[nodeId].route -- no hardcoded path construction
      needed since these verticals (unlike HC) already carry correct
      per-node URLs.
- Button template: fo/ins/con/re/leg/bpo docs now render the
  generative '↗ Open Node' button instead of a plain link (or nothing,
  for docs whose sourceNode didn't match a declared node key -- those
  previously showed no action at all).
- Verified: all 6 verticals have a real route on their war-room node,
  so targetUrl always resolves for these verticals; the null-route
  guard is defensive only.

Untouched: openHcNodeWithDoc and all __HC_NODE__ wiring -- purely
additive change, HC path unaffected.

Verified: node --check passes on server.js; all <script> blocks in
tsm-doc-search-multi.html parse cleanly via new Function().
